# wip362 / wip377: COPY-PASTE MODE: FUNC + ACCENT copies the pattern and the white keys wait.
# wip377: ONE paste: the white key pastes there, that pattern becomes the current one and the mode ENDS.
# FUNC pressed again (only FUNC) before choosing: the mode stays on, paste in many places; a button leaves.
# wip415: in the KEPT mode, FUNC + ACCENT again leaves it (nothing is copied).
wait 300
tap EDIT
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w8
# FUNC + ACCENT: copy pattern 1, the mode is on, not kept
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect clip 1
expect cpm 1
expect cpsticky 0
# one paste (pattern 4): the mode ends and pattern 4 is the current one (stopped: at once)
tapkey w3
expect cpm 0
expect pattern 4
expect hit0.0.0 1
expect hit0.0.8 1
# a white key now is a normal key again: no paste, mode off
tapkey w5
expect cpm 0
# the same, then FUNC pressed alone: the mode stays for many pastes
tap EDIT
key b10 down
tapkey w0
key b10 up
expect pattern 1
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
tapkey b10
expect cpm 1
expect cpsticky 1
tapkey w3
expect cpm 1
expect pattern 1
tapkey w5
expect cpm 1
expect pattern 1
# a button leaves the mode
tap EDIT
expect cpm 0
expect cpsticky 0
# FUNC HELD + white key is still the pattern change (the mode is not touched, not kept)
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
key b10 down
tapkey w6
expect pattern 7
expect cpsticky 0
key b10 up
expect cpsticky 0
tap EDIT
expect cpm 0
# FUNC + ACCENT + white key 6 (still held): pattern 6 is the copy (clip 6), then key 2 pastes it there and the mode ends
key b10 down
key b8 down
tapkey w5
key b8 up
key b10 up
expect clip 6
expect cpm 1
tapkey w1
expect cpm 0
expect pattern 2
# wip364: the blue hint and the lit key (screenshot); the playing pattern's key is the steady one
tap EDIT
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
wait 100
shot cpmode.png
tapkey b10
wait 100
shot cpmode_many.png
tap EDIT
expect cpm 0
# wip415: the kept mode, then FUNC + ACCENT again = the mode ends, the copy is not changed
tap EDIT
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
tapkey b10
expect cpm 1
expect cpsticky 1
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 0
expect cpsticky 0
# a white key is a normal key again (no paste)
tapkey w3
expect cpm 0
# not kept: FUNC + ACCENT again still copies again (the mode restarts, as before)
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
expect cpsticky 0
tap EDIT
expect cpm 0
# wip422: SEQ pressed in the mode leaves it and opens the SEQUENCER page (never the pattern page)
# (a) started on the SEQ page itself (before: SEQ again = the pattern page)
tap SEQ
expect seqpat 0
expect view 7
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
tap SEQ
expect cpm 0
expect seqpat 0
expect view 7
expect arp 0
# (b) from another page: the mode is on, SEQ goes to the sequencer page
tap EDIT
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
expect cpm 1
tap SEQ
expect cpm 0
expect seqpat 0
expect view 7
# (c) afterwards SEQ is normal again: 2nd press = the pattern page, 3rd = back
tap SEQ
expect seqpat 1
tap SEQ
expect seqpat 0
